# Phase 3 (D1) — every test context in this module talks to one JVM-scoped Testcontainers MySQL.
# The ApplicationContextInitializer entry covers raw SpringApplication runs; the
# ContextCustomizerFactory entry covers @SpringBootTest / TestContext contexts.
#
# Phase 5 (D7) — the same two entries for Redis. spring-boot-starter-data-redis puts a
# RedisHealthIndicator on the classpath, so /actuator/health would report DOWN without a
# reachable server, and the fail-closed limiter would reject every auth request in the suite.
# See TestRedis for the full reasoning.
org.springframework.context.ApplicationContextInitializer=\
com.healthcare.hms.db.TestDatabaseContextInitializer,\
com.healthcare.hms.db.TestRedisContextInitializer
org.springframework.test.context.ContextCustomizerFactory=\
com.healthcare.hms.db.TestDatabaseContextCustomizerFactory,\
com.healthcare.hms.db.TestRedisContextCustomizerFactory,\
com.healthcare.hms.db.TestRateLimitContextCustomizerFactory
